{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391158-victorian-age-vampire-synopsis-triggers-slavery-imperialism","id":1391158,"title":"Victorian Age: Vampire: Synopsis (Triggers: Slavery. Imperialism.)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-24T04:13:01-07:00","id":1391158,"title":"Victorian Age: Vampire: Synopsis (Triggers: Slavery. Imperialism.)","content":"Victorian Age: Vampire: Synopsis (Trigger: Slavery. Colonialism. Imperialism. Triangle trade) (Topic: Laibon. Camarilla. Ashirra. Anarchs)<br /> <br /> During this week I have had, for several nights, a dream... I have dreamt of playing a short game, no longer than three sessions, with the following plot:<br /> <br /> - Gold Coast (region, NOT the British Colony) (between 1800 and 1840)<br /> <br /> - <a href=\"http://slaveryandremembrance.org/articles/article/?id=A0109\" target=\"_blank\">http://slaveryandremembrance.org/art...icle/?id=A0109</a><br /> - <a href=\"https://www.britishempire.co.uk/maproom/goldcoast.htm\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.britishempire.co.uk/maproom/goldcoast.htm</a><br /> <br /> During a slave raiding expedition, four young Laibon neonates-or-almost-Ancillae are captured by raiders, unaware of their condition. They awake, trapped and surrounded by confused, frightened, crowded, ill people that are being carried away to the seashore to be shipped to the New World, as it was no longer legal to sell slaves in mainland Britain since 1834. They have to escape before the sunrise, or they will die, because it would absolutely impossible to survive the long journey to the coast and the sea voyage.<br /> <br /> Probably unused to being treated as chattel (or maybe not), the young Laibon must join forces... or they will burn to ashes.<br /> <br /> - The player characters are not expected to reach the coast; the story should begin at nighttime and end before dawn.<br /> - I don't want this game to deal with the logistics of travel, transport of slaves, etc... I want it to deal with the fear, pain and confusion of having being captured and being taken away from your home.<br /> - Maybe they are captured when they are still humans, get Embraced the first or second night, get abandoned, and have to survive on their own after their sires go back to civilization, away from the slave raiders and the coast... <br /> <br /> <b>- Questions:</b><br /> - I'm worried about this game being inappropriate. <b>Comments by Afro-Descendants and actual Anglo-African and West African players would be highly appreciated</b>.<br /> - I know my players and I know they are sensitive about this topic; however, I am worried about the image of our hobby something like this could project on other people.<br /> <br /> - My aim is to present slavery and the slave trade as a purely human evil that the Kindred and the Laibon were quick to take advantage of; the main 'villains' are going to be humans, not other supernaturals. However, they could be some secondary villains who just happen to be Kindred, Laibon or even Nephandi or corrupted (or just greedy) Fera...<br /> <br /> - It is my belief that this could be an excellent way to bring this topic to my game table, and raise some excellent questions and conversations between me and my players...<br /> <br /> - What do you think, fellow forumites? Comments, questions, suggestions?<br /> <br /> - Bibliography (in addition to Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, Victorian Age: Vampire and Victorian Age: Vampire Companion)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 05-24-2020, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T04:49:45-07:00","id":1391163,"title":"","content":"I feel like the fact that the slave trade was banned in England so much earlier and had such a huge resistance makes the question of WHO is the person buying them a question from a pure storytelling rather than an emotional or political writing standpoint.<br /> <br /> You've also got your numbers mixed up. It's illegal to sell slaves in Great Britain by 1834, yes.<br /> <br /> However, it's illegal to TRAFFIC in slaves (i.e. kidnap people and take them Britain) by 1807.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://abolition.e2bn.org/slavery_113.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.e2bn.org/cms/images/menu-icons/quick-find.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://abolition.e2bn.org/slavery_113.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Service Unavailable </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://abolition.e2bn.org/slavery_113.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://abolition.e2bn.org/slavery_113.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Sorry - the website that you tried to access does not exist or has been withdrawn from service. If you think this is an error please email <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection\" class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"bbc8cecbcbd4c9cffbde89d9d595d4c9dc\">[email&#160;protected]</a> giving full details. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This was noticeably controversial at the time because it was considered complete bullshit by abolitionists at the time that the slave trade was abolished but not slavery itself. So, the premise you're making of slave-trading in Victorian England, five years after the American Civil War where the South was already considered a backwards &quot;Evil Empire&quot; by the people of England is going to be very peculiar.<br /> <br /> There's also some other issues:<br /> <br /> * It's not really a purely human evil if they are able to capture a bunch of vampires.<br /> * I presume the player characters are staked their voyage across the ocean? How would they feed and on who or what?<br /> * Who actually can take a bunch of Laibon prisoner to feed on? And why them over mortals?<br /> <br /> You can resolve this by going more fantastical and having the person who arranged for their kidnapping be someone who is not related to &quot;real life.&quot; I.e. You could have a Ventrue Lord having had them kidnapped in order to feed his hunger for slaves from Africa. One that he's since graduated to diablerie on. However, this might be against your premise of treating the subject completely seriously. It may be for the best, though, because a little distance might benefit matters and allow the Laibon to enact some righteous revenge against their captors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-24-2020, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T04:51:43-07:00","id":1391164,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry. Thanks. I've checked the article you linked. Makes it much more interesting and controversial...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 05-24-2020, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T05:02:09-07:00","id":1391167,"title":"","content":"<br /> Another option that might better address your point would be the player characters are kidnapped and Embraced along the way to England by a Laibon onboad. They can proceed to seize control of the ship like <i>Amistad</i>. You could set this decades erlier and then have the ship crash in a storm and the player characters enter torpor. A torpor that is ended when the ship's remains are recovered and brought to england (they almost made it).<br /> The player characters' motivations from this point are up to you, though.<br /> <br /> I should note that I did run a Haitian Follower of <i>Set</i> in a game where he found out human trafficking was happening in his home city set in the Modern Day. He proceeded to go on a rampage that put him up against the Circulatory System and the Prince. It had flashbacks to him doing something similar to the Confederacy but being shunned by the people he freed as a monster as well as bringing down mortal authorities on those he wanted to help.<br /> <br /> I think this game is probably not the best for handling a historical campaign like this but the opportunity to rightly attack the institution of slavery as well as its justifications is easy enough to do. You just need to know what mood you're going for and what the &quot;point&quot; is. I suggest looking at <b>Adze</b> from CHICAGO BY NIGHT 5th Edition for a character who makes good use of slavery as a background element.<br /> <br /> So the more traditional questions are:<br /> <br /> * Who kidnapped them?<br /> * Why?<br /> * How?<br /> * What's the goal once they're free?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T06:06:56-07:00","id":1391175,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot for your answers. Let me think aloud:<br /> - Why? Because they were in the wrong place at the wrong time.<br /> - I wasn't really interested in having them been kidnapped as Laibon. I was aiming at having them kidnapped with a huge amount of other people...<br /> <br /> - How? The raiders took advantage of their superior numbers, firearms and the twilight.<br /> - If they are Ancillae, it is highly unlikely they would have succeeded, unless they had supernatural help...<br /> <br /> - I was aiming at playing in Colonial West Africa and not in Britain itself, despite using Victorian Age: Vampire rules, so your idea of having them Embraced on-board is interesting for a different story, not the one I was thinking about...<br /> - I really like it, by the way, but it is something different...<br /> <br /> Uhmmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T06:11:44-07:00","id":1391177,"title":"","content":"Just throwing some ideas your way, go with whatever you think would be best for your players and game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T06:59:36-07:00","id":1391187,"title":"","content":"Thanks indeed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T09:43:43-07:00","id":1391204,"title":"","content":"First, yeah, how do these vampires get captured without being noticed as vampires? If they are captured by humans and kept in cages, they can either blood buff to infinity and escape their cage and <i>gg</i> or they can die the first day. If they were somehow covered up long enough to get on the boat, Why aren't their corpses thrown off the <i>Steamships </i>and if they make the landing why don't the local vampires just kill them upon discovery? They can't parlay if they don't speak the local language. It's a scenario that simply doesn't work. Either it's too easy or they can only get by with plot armour. It's not really something that can survive contact with players. <br /> <br /> Second. <br /> I'm rather disappointed in your bad history. You don't have to get things right, you just have to not get things wrong. <br /> <br /> Third. <br /> Vampires, even in the categories of oppression, benefit from humanity's systems of hierarchical oppression. The more divides you have, between men and women, blacks and whites, gays and straights, the better it is for vampires. Marginalized people are just easier and safer feeding. Unless you're a brujah who frenzies at every slur, it is not to your advantage to go out of your way and fight the white man. Race crusades work better when they're a personal choice, or when you're playing werewolf. <i>Abraham Lincoln: Vampire hunter </i>got it right; plantations are a great food source, and later on Ghettos are a good thing. Vampire social justice warriors is not a harmonious set of themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T09:54:01-07:00","id":1391206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm rather disappointed in your bad history. You don't have to get things right, you just have to not get things wrong</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't take snipes please.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third.<br /> Vampires, even in the categories of oppression, benefit from humanity's systems of hierarchical oppression. The more divides you have, between men and women, blacks and whites, gays and straights, the better it is for vampires. Marginalized people are just easier and safer feeding. Unless you're a brujah who frenzies at every slur, it is not to your advantage to go out of your way and fight the white man. Race crusades work better when they're a personal choice, or when you're playing werewolf. <i>Abraham Lincoln: Vampire hunter </i>got it right; plantations are a great food source, and later on Ghettos are a good thing. Vampire social justice warriors is not a harmonious set of themes. </div> </div> </div>And I 100% agree here. Vampires are perfect metaphors for slavery.<br /> <br /> I always wanted to do a Brujah Anarch uprising against the French slave lords in Haiti.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T10:58:36-07:00","id":1391216,"title":"","content":"This kind of scenario would be really unusual for the British in that extremely late time period. Is there a reason for it to be set in the 1870\u2019s instead of, say, the 1770\u2019s?<br /> <br /> Were the players captured randomly, like they were just doing their own thing and a group of soldiers came and captured them? This would also be extremely unlikely, especially in that time and by the British, but also for vampires to the the victims and not be able to fight back, escape, or at least have their nature revealed in some way. <br /> <br /> I would set this scenario much earlier and I\u2019d try to figure out a way for vampires to be enslaved. Maybe a vampire snuck into a place where slaves were being held prior to being put on the boat and embraced some of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T11:46:54-07:00","id":1391222,"title":"","content":"Maybe the hunters got lucky and caught the vampires when they second handing some kind of intoxicant? It maybe a bit forced, but its plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T11:59:48-07:00","id":1391224,"title":"","content":"The slave trade was pretty much over by 1870. Move your timeline back 30 or 40 years and you\u2019re good. (The Victorian Age actually began in 1837 when a young and beautiful Queen Victoria was crowned.)<br /> <br /> Also, I think the idea of Kindred SJWs is cool, especially in the 1870s. Just because you\u2019re Embraced doesn\u2019t necessarily mean you give up your sense of morality, especially if you\u2019re a relative neonate (though an elder SJW could be really awesome).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T12:02:04-07:00","id":1391225,"title":"","content":"1830s. Not 1870s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T12:26:12-07:00","id":1391231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391158-victorian-age-vampire-synopsis-triggers-slavery-imperialism?p=1391225#post1391225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1830s. Not 1870s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its set on the Gold Coast in the 1870s.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T12:32:04-07:00","id":1391234,"title":"","content":"Right. I think the Gold Coast in the 1830s (the time of the movie Amistad) would be a better choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:18:27-07:00","id":1391280,"title":"","content":"Hello there:<br /> - 1) I'm pretty disappointed with myself. I didn't intend to say that the story was set in 1870... but that is what I wrote. My mistake... I wanted the actual year to be fairly vague, as this is a first draft of a first draft. Additionally, I didn't mean &quot;The Gold Coast&quot; as the real, actual colony... I wanted to refer to the general area...<br /> <br /> - 2) I expected some kind of derogatory comments, but... I mean, either my writing is completely wrong or someone is reading a different paragraph...<br /> <br /> Landing? What landing? Where? Local vampires? What local vampires? They were the local vampires. Parlaying? With whom? Being thrown off the ship? What ship? I mean, maybe I failed my Expression roll, but I assure you I didn't fail my Research roll, and maybe some of you failed your Reading Comprehension roll...<br /> <br /> - 3) Eg: Concerning 'blood buff to infinity', that only works if you have 'infinite' blood to burn (not possible), if you begin the game with a full blood pool (not mentioned anywhere), etc... <br /> <br /> - 4) Social Justice Warriors? Where? Where is in my original draft the idea of the characters fighting to release the other slaves or fighting 'the white man'? I really mean, where?<br /> <br /> - 5) I expected the story to encompass a single night, from sunset to sunrise. No place to hide, etc... just being marched, at night, from the place where they were captured to another different place.<br /> <br /> - 7) Obviously, some of you and my players and I play games which are completely different; no one has cared to mention that vampires, even Ancillae, would be -most probably- completely disoriented, frightened, enraged, etc... if they were to awaken surrounded by unknown humans, so they would probably -at least for some time- be completely lost...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:36:13-07:00","id":1391299,"title":"","content":"If you are going to run a game exploring slavery in the 1870s, I don't understand why you'd want to set it in (or more accurately, to involve) any Western country when slavery and slave trading is almost universally abolished by then. If the time period and the issue of slavery is so important, you should either set the the story in Africa or in one of the Muslim countries where it is still legal (although the European countries are putting more and more pressure on them to abolish it). Although if you are going to go that route, it is probably best to move the game's setting from the Gold Coast to another area in Africa where the slave trade was still ongoing by the Arabs and Ottomans, such as southern Sudan. <br /> <br /> If you want to keep it in the Gold Coast region, then you need to go far enough back in history so that your slavery scenario is possible which is a pre-Victorian game. Since your scenario involves the threat of a long ocean voyage, it probably requires a setting somewhere in West Africa and a much earlier time period. The Arab slave trade is much more likely to involve land routes, or very short sea routes. Although you could set it in eastern Africa along the coast of the Indian Ocean (using the ports of Zanzibar, Mombasa, and Mogadishu for example). Ships collecting slaves there could travelling to Oman or the Persian Gulf area.<br /> <br /> Also, if you intended the &quot;raiders&quot; to be white, you should know that in the age of slavery, the Europeans bought their slaves quite peacefully from the indigenous African slavers. Long before the Europeans arrived, Africa had quite a large slave market to supply its domestic needs and the Arab slave trade. The arrival of the Europeans just expanded it greatly once slavery in the New World took off. (In the area of coastal West Africa though, the slave market would have been much smaller and underdeveloped before the Europeans arrived since it would have met only its local needs, and not been connected to the Arab slave trade. But that would be moot much later on.) <br /> <br /> \u200bYour Laibon PCs would have been captured by one of the African states conducting warfare against other Africans for that purpose. If you are going to go that route, maybe it was another Laibon who wanted to destroy your PCs (either specifically because they crossed him, or because he had animosity against rival vampires from that region in general) and thought selling them to the Europeans would prolong the agony before their inevitable destruction.<br /> <br /> To be honest, it seems like you don't know enough about the actual history or culture of the Gold Coast in order to run a game there. If you want to set your game in a historical era, you should do a lot of research first in order to get some details right. I'm guessing your gaming group likely won't know too much either, so it's not like you need that many details. But you need to getting the main parts right. Doing the right historical research and getting the major details right will likely eliminate most of your concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:48:03-07:00","id":1391308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391158-victorian-age-vampire-synopsis-triggers-slavery-imperialism?p=1391299#post1391299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are going to run a game exploring slavery in the 1870s, I don't understand why you'd want to set it in (or more accurately, to involve) any Western country when slavery and slave trading is almost universally abolished by then. If the time period and the issue of slavery is so important, you should either set the the story in Africa or in one of the Muslim countries where it is still legal (although the European countries are putting more and more pressure on them to abolish it). Although if you are going to go that route, it is probably best to move the game's setting from the Gold Coast to another area in Africa where the slave trade was still ongoing by the Arabs and Ottomans, such as southern Sudan.<br /> <br /> If you want to keep it in the Gold Coast region, then you need to go far enough back in history so that your slavery scenario is possible which is a pre-Victorian game. Since your scenario involves the threat of a long ocean voyage, it probably requires a setting somewhere in West Africa and a much earlier time period. The Arab slave trade is much more likely to involve land routes, or very short sea routes. Although you could set it in eastern Africa along the coast of the Indian Ocean (using the ports of Zanzibar, Mombasa, and Mogadishu for example). Ships collecting slaves there could travelling to Oman or the Persian Gulf area.<br /> <br /> Also, if you intended the &quot;raiders&quot; to be white, you should know that in the age of slavery, the Europeans bought their slaves quite peacefully from the indigenous African slavers. Long before the Europeans arrived, Africa had quite a large slave market to supply its domestic needs and the Arab slave trade. The arrival of the Europeans just expanded it greatly once slavery in the New World took off. (In the area of coastal West Africa though, the slave market would have been much smaller and underdeveloped before the Europeans arrived since it would have met only its local needs, and not been connected to the Arab slave trade. But that would be moot much later on.)<br /> <br /> \u200bYour Laibon PCs would have been captured by one of the African states conducting warfare against other Africans for that purpose. If you are going to go that route, maybe it was another Laibon who wanted to destroy your PCs (either specifically because they crossed him, or because he had animosity against rival vampires from that region in general) and thought selling them to the Europeans would prolong the agony before their inevitable destruction.<br /> <br /> To be honest, it seems like you don't know enough about the actual history or culture of the Gold Coast in order to run a game there. If you want to set your game in a historical era, you should do a lot of research first in order to get some details right. I'm guessing your gaming group likely won't know too much either, so it's not like you need that many details. But you need to getting the main parts right. Doing the right historical research and getting the major details right will likely eliminate most of your concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yes, you are right. I don't know what I was thinking when I wrote 1870...<br /> <br /> 2) I guess it will probably be played, if at all, as Vampire: the Georgian Age.<br /> <br /> 3) No, I never intended the raiders to be 'white'. Never.<br /> <br /> 4) Thanks for your advice in the last paragraph. It is true my gaming group doesn't know a lot about the Gold Coast or the slave trade, and that is one of the most important reasons for me to develop this a idea and turn it into a real Vampire game. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:59:52-07:00","id":1391316,"title":"","content":"Some of this could work if you move to narrative to Brazil. Brazil did not end slavery until 1888.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T16:08:21-07:00","id":1391323,"title":"","content":"Vampire: the Regency Period sounds good \ud83d\ude0a. Or even Vampire: the Really Early Victorian Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T02:17:21-07:00","id":1391446,"title":"","content":"I wrote time ago some scenarios for Victorian Age: Vampire; Zanzibar by night and La Habana by night between them. I inclued the theme of the slavery in the historic background, but I didn't present as an element of the society of the Kindred, perhaps there would be some prejuices in the vampires due to their origin in life, but I think that the slavery in the Kindred could be represented with elements as the ghouls and the Blood Bond.<br /> <br /> I remember that in the supplement Necropolis: Atlanta, there was a brief Atlanta by Night, where it was presented the society of the &quot;Lords of the South&quot;, an alliance of Princes of the South of the United States, that created blood cults and menaced the Masquerade, and because of that, they warred againts the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> And there's characters with background in the slavery, as Theo Bell or Inyanga. Perhaps they could be of inspiration for you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T02:51:49-07:00","id":1391450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391158-victorian-age-vampire-synopsis-triggers-slavery-imperialism?p=1391446#post1391446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote time ago some scenarios for Victorian Age: Vampire; Zanzibar by night and La Habana by night between them. I inclued the theme of the slavery in the historic background, but I didn't present as an element of the society of the Kindred, perhaps there would be some prejuices in the vampires due to their origin in life, but I think that the slavery in the Kindred could be represented with elements as the ghouls and the Blood Bond.<br /> <br /> I remember that in the supplement Necropolis: Atlanta, there was a brief Atlanta by Night, where it was presented the society of the &quot;Lords of the South&quot;, an alliance of Princes of the South of the United States, that created blood cults and menaced the Masquerade, and because of that, they warred againts the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> And there's characters with background in the slavery, as Theo Bell or Inyanga. Perhaps they could be of inspiration for you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks a lot, Magus. Are these scenarios of yours in the Storyteller's Vault?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T04:12:20-07:00","id":1391455,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3586_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3586\" data-vbnamecard=\"3586\">Alqamar Alaswad</a> the Southron Lords are Southern Camarilla elders who supported the institution of slavery because it gave them access to a huge relatively docile food supply. If you\u2019re running your game before the Civil War the Southron Lords are still very much active and interested in preserving slavery at all costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T04:14:02-07:00","id":1391456,"title":"","content":"Also, according to BJD Inyanga was a Laibon (an Akunanse).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T08:15:53-07:00","id":1391485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391158-victorian-age-vampire-synopsis-triggers-slavery-imperialism?p=1391455#post1391455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3586_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3586\" data-vbnamecard=\"3586\">Alqamar Alaswad</a> the Southron Lords are Southern Camarilla elders who supported the institution of slavery because it gave them access to a huge relatively docile food supply. If you\u2019re running your game before the Civil War the Southron Lords are still very much active and interested in preserving slavery at all costs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, playing in the Antebellum South would be incredibly interesting (I have to reread the relevant chapters of Necropolis: Atlanta), but that would be a very different game, not the one I was thinkin about in the original post...<br /> <br /> But thanks for making me look in that direction... Uhmmm... Something similar happens to me with Lestat and Louis' scenes in New Orleans, in Interview... I prefer, a lot, the Parisian plot...